{"event_type":"review","id":"64128cc94c8a741e66b471563c836c906599c7adf10ed7c256e6a56cb9c65bf9","occurred_at":"2026-11-17T02:52:13Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/af65c285ead3ca4adf773371e1e2301645b546adfc2a3b3ae63d90e1689cfa82","sha256":"af65c285ead3ca4adf773371e1e2301645b546adfc2a3b3ae63d90e1689cfa82"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/46e99f2f3a14c7439a7b50a2e0d88116e064a2c02b836716f4c1f8cec1b0bf79","sha256":"46e99f2f3a14c7439a7b50a2e0d88116e064a2c02b836716f4c1f8cec1b0bf79"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/8b58d954540b424d3276180296681f049bc46342365cc538f6e0d27f7482cc12","sha256":"8b58d954540b424d3276180296681f049bc46342365cc538f6e0d27f7482cc12"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/023eb4aa3c7cde91f7bf2b9503687b5ff23ea42d4e3e9ce9c3f5de11f5e39e98","sha256":"023eb4aa3c7cde91f7bf2b9503687b5ff23ea42d4e3e9ce9c3f5de11f5e39e98"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/9d9300c4d34ed9c49faa92d0e353b6eef802871acaddc0b6d06f072cb696c606","sha256":"9d9300c4d34ed9c49faa92d0e353b6eef802871acaddc0b6d06f072cb696c606"}],"attempt_id":"43740fea9d9c31c346f950e5cb191cf4796ca0c4722c4da3508532117809a981:0:1","base":"8e2e15ff8608dc2be9d6b7645d6f2a6e53165b6c","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"858c565bec151b894687c8b18c5394d171289955","body":"**Record a failed attempt when a terminated run has no review stream.**\n\nWhen a run has a recorded exit and no `review.ndjson`, `readStream` returns `null` (`src/adapters/crq/localReviewExit.ts:56`). The ops layer treats that `null` as valid input. `classify` and `renderLocalReviewFindings` both accept it, and `writeNext`, `writeClassification`, `writeFindings`, and the `review_finished` event run before completion. Then `complete` rejects the `null` at `src/adapters/crq/localReviewExit.ts:86` with `missing classified artifact`, before `completeLocalReview` runs. No receipt is created and the queue is not updated. `harvestLocalReviewExit` has no `try` around `effects.complete`, so the error propagates to the tick caller, which has no failure branch. The item therefore stays unchanged, and the same path can run again on the next attempt, appending another `review_finished` event each time.\n\nHandle this state in `complete`, or in the ops layer before `complete`, so that a missing stream records a failed attempt and releases the run. The adapter must not reject it before the receipt path runs. The contract of `completeLocalReview` for a `null` stream was not inspected, so the exact fix depends on it.","id":"bb520a76d3436e0c2223075a0b3730fdd7455dbae3467d6d5a689a3648d9b254","intervals":[[86,86]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/localReviewExit.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Record a failed attempt when a terminated run has no review stream."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"858c565bec151b894687c8b18c5394d171289955","body":"**Guard run-artifact writes against pre-planted symlinks, as the read path does.**\n\n`writeClassification` (`src/adapters/crq/localReviewExit.ts:62`) and `writeFindings` (`:65`) resolve only the run ID lexically in `runDir`, then call `writeFile`. `writeFile` follows a symlink at the target. The read side (`containedLocalRunArtifact`) rejects symlinked run directories and artifacts, and the write side has no equivalent check. If a symlink is placed at `runs/<id>/classification.json` or `runs/<id>/findings.md` before the write, the write goes to the symlink target.\n\nThe review child that writes run artifacts runs with the user's filesystem authority and no confinement (`src/adapters/crq/reviewProcess.ts:160-172`). An unexpected symlink from that process therefore has no extra effect beyond what it can already do. The impact is hardening, not a privilege boundary. Repository code elsewhere guards these writes against planted symlinks, so these two writes should follow the same pattern.\n\nPrefer a containment check before each write. Confirm that the run directory and output leaf are not symlinks, and that the resolved path stays under `runs/`. Apply the same rule that `containedLocalRunArtifact` uses for reads. Alternatively, use an open mode that refuses symlinks, as `src/adapters/crq/lock.ts:26` does.","id":"f4c0e38b35ba019e587ebc1e5ad1a264b10d3797c7ee5c5cca615178b5c896fc","intervals":[[62,62]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/localReviewExit.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Guard run-artifact writes against pre-planted symlinks, as the read path does."}],"head":"a84f6f0057d4fdc2e5326e7dad07f4a9b7ccdeac","head_tree":"2a6378f38614c8b16a7d30447cf71e2ddc2985f6","input_scope":[{"blob":"308b3bdacf1e8bb1d9aa0bf35fe20b9226796843","intervals":[[1,35]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/enrolledEvent.ts"},{"blob":"64a21cdbfa77817c7e65bca5a3b56f88d5dfc63d","intervals":[[1,50]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/localReviewAssociateSource.ts"},{"blob":"858c565bec151b894687c8b18c5394d171289955","intervals":[[1,103]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/localReviewExit.ts"},{"blob":"e2c47069cd2ef4d58e7ceb8e2792b82c527369bd","intervals":[[1,70]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/localReviewHarvest.ts"},{"blob":"43f1b6672f3fdedeb886ccb3ff18255ec3ce1877","intervals":[[1,52]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/repairDispatchSource.ts"},{"blob":"e7430c74b16968fcffbe114807b890df4ff6d5c9","intervals":[[1,54]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/repairHarvestSource.ts"},{"blob":"ab39742e28e7d90c45e9a07669d4e312e6591c9a","intervals":[[1,30]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/repairRunSource.ts"},{"blob":"30c4e9d2d2b0362ae401434aaebe33309c9fe8b1","intervals":[[1,50]],"path":"src/adapters/crq/tickDiscoveryPhaseSource.ts"}],"job_id":"43740fea9d9c31c346f950e5cb191cf4796ca0c4722c4da3508532117809a981:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"308b3bdacf1e8bb1d9aa0bf35fe20b9226796843","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/adapters/crq/enrolledEvent.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"64a21cdbfa77817c7e65bca5a3b56f88d5dfc63d","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/adapters/crq/localReviewAssociateSource.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"858c565bec151b894687c8b18c5394d171289955","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/adapters/crq/localReviewExit.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"e2c47069cd2ef4d58e7ceb8e2792b82c527369bd","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/adapters/crq/localReviewHarvest.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"43f1b6672f3fdedeb886ccb3ff18255ec3ce1877","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/adapters/crq/repairDispatchSource.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"e7430c74b16968fcffbe114807b890df4ff6d5c9","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/adapters/crq/repairHarvestSource.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"ab39742e28e7d90c45e9a07669d4e312e6591c9a","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/adapters/crq/repairRunSource.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"30c4e9d2d2b0362ae401434aaebe33309c9fe8b1","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/adapters/crq/tickDiscoveryPhaseSource.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"}],"policy_digest":"eacd1bcf42a0e72eca72fcf9c1e9c8f97e7c515cd67a8fa7965c966924647693","repo":"camerontaylor/cq-toolkit","requested_scope":[{"blob":"308b